      "content": "These criticisms argue that the Supreme Court has \"judicial activism,\" essentially \"legislating from the bench\" to create rights not explicitly stated in the Constitution. Proponents of the doctrine, however, argue that the \"unwritten\" rights, like privacy, are inherent to the concept of \"liberty\" in the Bill of Rights. In essence, the debate is over whether the Constitution is a strict, explicit rulebook or a framework that implies certain fundamental human rights for all its citizens to protect.",
